# Project exclude paths
/project/project/target/
/project/target/
/target/
/target/scala-3.4.1/classes/
.scala-build

.idea
.bsp

/scbuild/

/sc-run/
/scbuild/

.claude

/.tools/

# Python bytecode caches (scripts/ is imported as a package by the generators)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# REVIEW INPUTS, not artifacts.  An acceptance review handed to this tree is an input to the work,
# and plan.md is the tracked plan against it.  Keeping the input out of the tree also keeps
# scripts/check_references.py honest: it scans every TRACKED file, and a review document quotes
# paths and file names from the state it reviewed, several of which no longer exist by design.
/review.md

# run.sh's transient vacuity probe (it removes it; this stops a mid-run `git add -A` catching it)
proofs/unbounded/.probe.p

# The status-table staging files (0.1).  Every status harness now accumulates rows in
# `STATUS.tsv.tmp` beside its target and publishes with ONE rename(), so a killed run cannot
# truncate a committed corpus.  SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP are trapped and remove the staging file;
# SIGKILL cannot be, so a hard-killed run leaves one behind and it must not show up as an untracked
# file in the Phase-0 tree-clean gate (`git status --porcelain proofs/ terminating/`).  The next run
# truncates it, so a stale one is inert.
STATUS.tsv.tmp

# THE LEAN BUILD DIRECTORY (0.5).  `proofs/lean/.lake` holds three things, none of which belongs in
# the tree: lake's build outputs (`.olean`/`.ilean`/`.c`), the generated `*.setup.json` files (which
# embed ABSOLUTE paths — `scripts/check_references.py` flagged 40-odd of them on the first run), and
# `packages/`, the Mathlib checkout, which is several gigabytes.
#
# WHAT IS TRACKED IS THE PIN, and only the pin: `proofs/lean/lean-toolchain` (the Lean version),
# `proofs/lean/lakefile.toml` (Mathlib's `rev`) and `proofs/lean/lake-manifest.json` (the resolved
# commit).  A reader who checks out this tree runs `lake update && lake exe cache get` and gets the
# same Mathlib; `scripts/check_lean.sh` refuses to build against a toolchain the pin does not name.
proofs/lean/.lake/
# `scripts/check_lean.sh`'s transient `#print axioms` probe (it removes it; this stops a
# SIGKILLed run, or a mid-run `git add -A`, from catching it).
proofs/lean/.axioms_probe.lean

# A6: the transfer checker's inputs, written by `sbt "testOnly morkl.SpatialTransferDump"` (see proofs/spatial/README.md)
proofs/spatial/out/
